cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the AVBD sandbox guest it is vendored from.
title: AVBD sandbox guest (vendored)
abstract: >-
  The AVBD CPU guest from V-Sekai-fire/interactor-mujoco-sandbox-demo
  (guest-avbd): the Lean-generated kernels driven by AvbdCpu, the Eigen-free
  predictor/velocity/grab driver (avbd_sim.h), the panel mesh builder
  (cloth_grid) and slangc's cpp prelude (slang-rt). Adapted here: params
  blocks follow Lean HEAD (count guards, dual-update beta/penaltyMax), the
  topology (CSR, colouring) is shared with AvbdRd through avbd_topology, the
  driver is templated over the backend, and run()/sync()/numColors() give
  AvbdCpu the same surface as AvbdRd. The kernels themselves are not vendored;
  kernels/avbd/gen.sh regenerates them from cloth-dynamics lean (vendored as
  lean/ in the next commit).


  Ported from cloth-dynamics src/code/slang_solver/AvbdSolverVk.cpp (see
  references; line numbers at that commit) into avbd_cpu_backward.cpp,
  avbd_rd_backward.cpp and avbd_rd.cpp. The reverse-mode stepBackward
  (ensureBackwardBuffers 1450-1523, stepBackward 1525-1649, the read*Grad
  accessors 1651-1723): the kernel sequence and bindings are kept, the
  force backwards see the pre-step positions (1552); adapted, the host
  prologue deltaX = positions - positionsPre (1530-1545) and the host
  epilogue vPosGrad += vPosInit + vOut (1636-1647) run as the Lean-emitted
  saxpby kernel on both backends, and runWithBackward records the forward
  iterations and the backward in one submit. The self-collision scan
  (SelfCollisionScanParams 807-810, uploadSelfCollisionRadii and
  detectSelfCollisions 1377-1411): adapted, detectSelfCollisions is split
  into submitSelfCollisionScan and collectSelfCollisions so the readback
  lands on a later frame (AGENTS.md rule 4); AvbdRd keeps no one-call form.
  The ragged-tail padding (rationale 23-32, roundUp/capacityFor 62-63, the
  per-colour vertPerm padding 905-916, index padding to the dummy vertex with
  zero stiffness 1028-1031 and at every capacityFor allocation 969-1193):
  kept on AvbdRd, which pads every vertex and constraint buffer to
  roundUp(n+1, 64) with pad indices at vertex nV and identity rows in
  hScratch; adapted, setPadFillForTest repoints the padding at a real vertex
  for the negative control. The pre-step snapshot (1241-1247, positions only
  upstream): adapted, AvbdRd copies positions with buffer_copy on the GPU,
  and both backends also snapshot the triangle and bending duals
  (lambda0/lambda1/lambda) before each step and bind the copies in the
  backward (setLambdaSnapshotForTest binds the live duals for the control).
  The two AL backward kernels never read the duals, so this changes no
  output today; it keeps the binding right if a kernel starts to.
type: software
